ff, review ratio or additional gate is supplied here.\\n' +\n  '  18  \\n' +\n  '  19  Bind the exact claim, affected subject and basis, existing grant, carrier,\\n' +\n  '  20  applicable obligations, actors and decision owner, evidence and stop conditions.\\n' +\n  '  21  Use a sufficient direct Writer where the accepted configuration permits one.\\n' +\n  '  22  Use coordination only for the material authority, dependency, capability or\\n' +\n  '  23  attention boundary that requires it; adopt the optional Executive profile\\n' +\n  '  24  separately. Sources: [ACTIVATION §1](ACTIVATION.md#1-the-step),\\n' +\n  '  25  [TICKETS §5](TICKETS.md#5-from-carrier-to-execution) and\\n' +\n  '  26  [EXECUTIVE_BASELINE §3](EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#3-engagement-applicability).\\n' +\n  '  27  \\n' +\n  '  28  ## Selected default flow\\n' +\n  '  29  \\n' +\n  '  30  1. **Recover the work reference and construct bounded context.** Start from\\n' +\n  '  31     the exact admitted ticket, sprint entry or run contract. Bind its current\\n' +\n  '  32     question, subject/basis, grant, result/evidence routes and surviving\\n' +\n  '  33     obligations. Apply [work continuity](#work-reference-context-and-continuation)\\n' +\n  '  34     below before relying on a summary or prior result. A new session alone\\n' +\n  '  35     neither resets progress nor requires another ticket.\\n' +\n  '  36  2. **Construct and perform incremental QA.** Check the admitted step against\\n' +\n  '  37     its requirement/design and the smallest adequate falsifier. State the\\n' +\n  '  38     observed predicate, subject, oracle, coverage and residuals. A local pass\\n' +\n  '  39     supports that bounded predicate; it supplies no unnamed Product acceptance,\\n' +\n  '  40     qualification or release claim. Preserve selected gates and mandatory\\n' +\n  '  41     conditions. Sources: [ASSURANCE](ASSURANCE.md),\\n' +\n  '  42     [EVALUATION §1](EVALUATION.md#1-claims) and\\n' +\n  '  43     [EVALUATION §5](EVALUATION.md#landing-closure-and-release).\\n' +\n  '  44  3. **Triage a discrepancy before selecting a repair.** Use the causal routes\\n' +\n  '  45     below and retain plausible unresolved causes. Repeated failure, escalating\\n' +\n  '  46     repair cost or growing review context calls for bounded diagnosis of the\\n' +\n  '  47     frame and capability; it authorizes neither another code patch nor an\\n' +\n  '  48     upstream change. Source: [SPEC_METHOD intake](SPEC_METHOD.md#universal-intake-triage).\\n' +\n  '  49  4. **Re-enter at the owning layer.** Record the change intent/class, affected\\n' +\n  '  50     Product boundary, first changed layer, downstream impact and whether release\\n' +\n  '  51     scope changes. Reuse the admitted ticket, sprint entry or run intake when\\n' +\n  '  52     it still covers the work. A changed requested outcome or territory needs\\n' +\n  '  53     owner re-entry and admission before dependent effects. Select `stdo-ticket`\\n' +\n  '  54     only when its durable-state need and effect grant hold; an unrelated finding\\n' +\n  '  55     does not silently enlarge this work. Sources: [change classes](SPEC_METHOD.md#change-classes),\\n' +\n  '  56     [TICKETS carrier selection](TICKETS.md#carrier-selection).\\n' +\n  '  57  5. **Repair, verify and dispose the bounded result.** Reconcile the affected\\n' +\n  '  58     requirement, design, implementation, tests and displaced path; retain\\n' +\n  '  59     unaffected valid support. Apply the verification and stopping rules below.\\n' +\n  '  60     The authorized decision owner chooses `accept`, `local_repair`, `re_enter`\\n' +\n  '  61     or `reject` under [ACTIVATION §3](ACTIVATION.md#disposition). Preserve the\\n' +\n  '  62     result and lawful next action through the named durable surface before\\n' +\n  '  63     return. A new scope or missing authority returns to that owner before\\n' +\n  '  64     continuation.\\n' +\n  '  65  \\n' +\n  '  66  ## Work reference, context and continuation\\n' +\n  '  67  \\n' +\n  '  68  The selected ticket is the enduring reference for its unit of work, under\\n' +\n  '  69  [TICKETS records](TICKETS.md#ticket-records) and\\n' +\n  '  70  [one-truth state](TICKETS.md#one-truth-state-projection-and-drift-refusal-up-009).\\n' +\n  '  71  Retain a sufficient sprint or run carrier where\\n' +\n  '  72  [carrier selection](TICKETS.md#carrier-selection) permits it. Work-state\\n' +\n  '  73  authority, governing meaning and current material evidence remain distinct;\\n' +\n  '  74  a context summary or index supplies none of them by itself.\\n' +\n  '  75  \\n' +\n  '  76  Acquire the deciding owners and current material subject needed by the next\\n' +\n  '  77  bounded decision. An accessible qualified reference must preserve the\\n' +\n  \"  78  consumer's subject/basis, assessment standing, provenance, active obligations\\n\" +\n  '  79  and invalidators. If a derived surface is stale or insufficient, re-enter the\\n' +\n  '  80  exact owning sections. Where the selected envelope declares context capacity,\\n' +\n  '  81  record the required measurement, capacity and comparison before reading.\\n' +\n  '  82  Without complete active inputs or a supported upper bound, complete-fit\\n' +\n  '  83  judgment remains unresolved unless a measured excess falsifies it. Where no\\n' +\n  '  84  capacity is declared, no measurement gate is added. Source:\\n' +\n  '  85  [ACTIVATION §2](ACTIVATION.md#2-context-construction-under-an-envelope).\\n' +\n  '  86  \\n' +\n  '  87  Before return, a permitted Writer records the closed result, step-produced\\n' +\n  '  88  facts needed later, evidence, unresolved work, original owner rulings and the\\n' +\n  '  89  next authorized action or owner re-entry in the existing named durable\\n' +\n  '  90  result/evidence surface. Keep references with the owning work. This projection\\n' +\n  '  91  adds no second state ledger or per-tool logging requirement. An actor without those effects\\n' +\n  '  92  returns to the permitted Writer; Executive still performs no file or Git\\n' +\n  '  93  mutation in that role. Sources:\\n' +\n  '  94  [ACTIVATION admission](ACTIVATION.md#admission),\\n' +\n  '  95  [closed results](ACTIVATION.md#7-closed-result-and-reuse),\\n' +\n  '  96  [TICKETS continuity](TICKETS.md#recorded-judgment-and-owner-ruling-continuity).\\n' +\n  '  97  \\n' +\n  '  98  Resume from current material state, correct a contrary retained account,\\n' +\n  '  99  check exact applicability and invalidators, and reopen only affected support.\\n' +\n  ' 100  Reconcile uncertain external effects before a retry or dependent action;\\n' +\n  ' 101  unresolved completion remains unresolved. Handoff needs sufficient closed\\n' +\n  \" 102  results and references, not the prior actor's private conversation. Sources:\\n\" +\n  ' 103  [ACTIVATION state and restart](ACTIVATION.md#5-work-state-and-restart),\\n' +\n  ' 104  [actor account](ACTIVATION.md#the-workspace-and-an-actors-account) and\\n' +\n  ' 105  [reuse](ACTIVATION.md#7-closed-result-and-reuse).\\n' +\n  ' 106  \\n' +\n  ' 107  ## Causal triage\\n' +\n  ' 108  \\n' +\n  ' 109  The four causes are owned by\\n' +\n  ' 110  [ACTIVATION feedback and diagnosis](ACTIVATION.md#construction-relation) and\\n' +\n  ' 111  applied by [SPEC_METHOD intake](SPEC_METHOD.md#universal-intake-triage).\\n' +\n  ' 112  Use evidence that distinguishes causes over the same exact subject and basis:\\n' +\n  ' 113  \\n' +\n  ' 114  | Supported cause | Lawful next action |\\n' +\n  ' 115  |---|---|\\n' +\n  ' 116  | Defective realisation under adequate unchanged law | Repair the realised surface within its grant; assert and verify no upstream drift. |\\n' +\n  ' 117  | Inadequate governing requirement or design | Return to the first inadequate owner; admit its changed truth, then derive affected downstream work and evidence. A failed candidate alone does not establish this cause. |\\n' +\n  \" 118  | Inaccurate predictive model | Return to the model's owner, identify the failed prediction and supported replacement/intervention, then re-evaluate the dependent claims. Do not relabel an outcome mismatch as a code defect without evidence. |\\n\" +\n  ' 119  | Insufficient observation | Acquire the missing admissible observation through its authorized route, or retain `indeterminate` and withhold the dependent claim. Repetition of the same uninformative check supplies no missing evidence. |\\n' +\n  ' 120  \\n' +\n  ' 121  If diagnosis or repair cannot fit the current capability/complexity envelope,\\n' +\n  ' 122  apply [REFERENCE_FRAME diagnostic order](REFERENCE_FRAME.md#diagnostic-order):\\n' +\n  ' 123  check the activated family, exact subject/basis, actor capability and available\\n' +\n  ' 124  evidence before missing variables, joins, families or another frame. Then\\n' +\n  ' 125  revise, decompose or request the capable evaluation through its owner. State\\n' +\n  ' 126  the missing relation/capability, next discriminating evidence and bounded\\n' +\n  ' 127  return condition. This route changes no requirement merely to make work pass.\\n' +\n  ' 128  \\n' +\n  ' 129  Keep technical severity and causal confidence separate from Product priority,\\n' +\n  ' 130  promotion effect and disposition. The Reviewer supplies supported triage and\\n' +\n  ' 131  explicit uncertainty; the Product decision owner decides its consequence under\\n' +\n  ' 132  the actual mandate. Under an adopted Executive profile that owner is the\\n' +\n  ' 133  Executive. Use the selected scale and preserve historical grades; severity\\n' +\n  ' 134  does not itself grant or forbid an operation. Sources:\\n' +\n  ' 135  [EVALUATION results](EVALUATION.md#result-and-triage-projection),\\n' +\n  ' 136  [blocking](EVALUATION.md#when-a-finding-blocks-promotion) and\\n' +\n  ' 137  [Executive triage](EXECUTIVE_BASELINE.md#technical-triage-severity-priority-and-boundary